  "body": "A linked model's SHA-256 now comes from the same read of the file that the import parsed. Before, the import read the file, parsed it, then read it again for the digest: a file that changed between the two reads recorded the newer digest over the older mesh, and the change was never imported (#2689, found in the review of #2563).\n\n## What changed\n\n- **One read** (`crates/app/src/geometry/import/sourced.rs`, new, native only): `load_model_open_sourced` returns the graded mesh and the digest of the bytes it parsed.\n  - OBJ, STEP and `.sc`: the buffer that is parsed is hashed.\n  - STL keeps its streaming parse (M5.3 E: the file never coexists with its triangles). A reader hashes every byte it hands to the parser. The ASCII path rewinds to byte 0 once after the sniff; the rewind starts the hash again. Any other seek is refused, so the digest is always of one pass. Bytes after the last binary facet, if the file grew, go into the same pass.\n  - Same size cap and the same verdicts as `load_model_open_within`, which stays for the browser build.\n- **`ImportModel::within`** uses it on native builds; the browser build records no link, as before.\n- **Kernel SHA-256 in pieces** (`crates/kernel/src/solidcraft/sha256.rs`): `Sha256::new / update / finish_hex`; `hex_digest` is that over one piece. Re-exported as `camcraft_geometry::solidcraft::Sha256`.\n- **The link check** (`model_source::read`) hashes the file in 1 MiB pieces. Before, it read the whole file into memory each time a linked file changed, which for a large STL broke the same memory law.\n- `stl.rs`: `parse_stream` and `READ_BUF_BYTES` become `pub(super)` for the new module; no other change (the file is over the line limit, so the new code is in its own file).\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/2689-one-read-digest.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/kernel/src/solidcraft/sha256.rs` `pieces_hash_as_the_whole`: every split (1, 3, 55, 64, 65, 200 bytes) of lengths around the 55/56/64-byte padding edges gives the one-shot digest. The FIPS 180-4 vectors still pass.\n- `crates/app/tests/model_link.rs`:\n  - `the_link_digest_is_of_the_one_read_the_import_parsed`: for an ASCII STL (the rewind path), a binary STL, OBJ and STEP, the import's digest and the check's streamed digest are the SHA-256 of the file.\n  - `the_link_check_hashes_a_file_larger_than_one_piece_as_a_whole`: a 3 MiB file, read in 1 MiB pieces.\n  - The 7 tests of #2463 still pass.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick` (as a separate user with no credentials): 898 steps, 0 failed. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-kernel -p camcraft-geometry -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The race itself is not reproduced by a test: it needs a write landing during a parse. The fix removes the second read by construction; the tests pin that the digest is of the parsed read.\n- Windows and Linux: not run. No platform branches.\n- The browser build (`wasm32`): `web/build-app-wasm.sh` fails on `main` today, before this PR, in the link check from #2463 (`model_link_watch.rs` takes `std::time::Instant`; E0308 at `state.rs:3130`). With that one-line fix on top (a separate PR), this branch builds for the browser: `web/build-app-wasm.sh` exit 0 (Homebrew clang 23 for wasm32).\n\nChangelog: A file that changes while CamCraft imports it is no longer missed: the linked model's digest is now of the bytes the import read (#2689).\nEffort: medium\nFork synced at v0.24.0 (branch from upstream main 3a240b7fb).\n\nFixes #2689\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01MLU9aif5zm7mure23AKftd\n",
